      "supplier_excerpts": [
        {
          "supplier": "cor-qft-example-scalar-tree-coefficients",
          "carrier": "items/cor-qft-example-scalar-tree-coefficients.md",
          "status": "Current QFT-MX02 draft corollary and full proof inspected.",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "exact_statement": "Let $m\\geq0$ be a scalar rest energy in joules and $s>4m^2$. For a specified dimensionless real quartic tree amplitude $\\mathcal A=-\\lambda$, the coefficient map of [[lem-qft-example-two-body-phase-space]] gives\n$$\\frac{d\\sigma_{\\mathrm{coeff}}}{d\\Omega} =\\frac{\\lambda^2(\\hbar c)^2}{128\\pi^2s}, \\qquad \\sigma_{\\mathrm{coeff}}=\\frac{\\lambda^2(\\hbar c)^2}{32\\pi s}$$\nfor identical final scalars integrated over the full labeled sphere. For distinguishable final scalars the two coefficients are twice these values.\n\nFor a parent at rest with energy $\\mathsf M_0>2m$ decaying to two identical scalars of rest energy $m$ under a specified constant amplitude $G_E$ in joules, the rate coefficient is\n$$\\Gamma_{\\mathrm{coeff}} =\\frac{|G_E|^2}{32\\pi\\hbar\\mathsf M_0} \\sqrt{1-\\frac{4m^2}{\\mathsf M_0^2}}.$$\nThis result concerns the defined formal coefficients. It does not assert an exact exponential survival law.",
