        "notes": "Read both steps and current scalar/phase-space suppliers, probability and Borel definitions, Lebesgue definition and Borel-measurability theorem with explicit AC_omega. Massless daughters satisfy the strict M0>0 threshold, G_E!=0 gives Gamma>0, and lambda=0 gives zero scattering without affecting lifetime. Renamed the restricted Lebesgue measure ell to remove its collision with real quartic lambda. Measurable T defines a countably additive pushforward; the separately assumed exponential density integrates to 1, its tail is exp(-Gamma t), its first moment is 1/Gamma and the unique half-life is ln(2)/Gamma. No observed sample, precision, or deductive lifetime implication from a rate alone. Outside scalar supplier hypothesis omission remains owner-routed."
      }
